From 3dbc8a1669b254cdee5823c8c154138ef0950b40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anders Kaseorg <andersk@mit.edu>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 22:31:00 +0000
Subject: don't misparse protected action frames as ADDBA requests

The TX paths look for ADDBA requests, to queue them on the access
category of their TID, by reading the action frame body right after
the 802.11 header. In a protected frame, however, that is where
mac80211 puts the CCMP header: always on the 88W8864, 88W8897 and
88W8997, which set IEEE80211_KEY_FLAG_GENERATE_IV, and on the 88W8964
once it sets IEEE80211_KEY_FLAG_GENERATE_IV_MGMT. The header starts
with the packet number, so a protected frame with PN 3 looks like an
ADDBA request whose capability bytes give TID 8, and utils_tid_to_ac()
returns -1. The frame then lands in txq[4], which the TX tasklet never
services, so of the protected management frames sent to each station,
the third one is never transmitted. (Once more than txq_limit frames
have accumulated there, ieee80211_stop_queue() would even be called
with queue -1.)

Skip protected frames. With PMF, ADDBA requests are protected anyway,
and mac80211 sends them with ieee80211_tx_skb_tid(), which already
selects the queue for the TID. Also don't use an invalid TID's -1 as a
queue index.

Seen on a WRT3200ACM (88W8964) with PMF: of the router's ADDBA requests
and SA Query requests to each station, the one with PN 3 was never
sent, and frames accumulated in txq[4].

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anders Kaseorg <andersk@mit.edu>
---
 hif/pcie/8864/tx.c     | 8 +++++++-
 hif/pcie/8964/tx_ndp.c | 8 +++++++-
 hif/pcie/8997/tx.c     | 8 +++++++-
 3 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/hif/pcie/8864/tx.c
+++ b/hif/pcie/8864/tx.c
@@ -717,13 +717,19 @@ void pcie_8864_tx_xmit(struct ieee80211_
 	if (mgmtframe) {
 		u16 capab;
 
+		/* The body of a protected frame starts with its CCMP
+		 * header (or is encrypted). mac80211 queues ADDBA requests
+		 * on the right AC anyway.
+		 */
 		if (unlikely(ieee80211_is_action(wh->frame_control) &&
+			     !ieee80211_has_protected(wh->frame_control) &&
 			     mgmt->u.action.category == WLAN_CATEGORY_BACK &&
 			     mgmt->u.action.action_code ==
 			     WLAN_ACTION_ADDBA_REQ)) {
 			capab = le16_to_cpu(mgmt->u.action.addba_req.capab);
 			tid = (capab & IEEE80211_ADDBA_PARAM_TID_MASK) >> 2;
-			index = utils_tid_to_ac(tid);
+			if (tid < IEEE80211_FIRST_TSPEC_TSID)
+				index = utils_tid_to_ac(tid);
 		}
 	}
 
